def memory_support_reader():
    """How much of an answer the memory's own writing carries, as a share of it.

    An answer is written out of the strings the memory writes, and two derivations of one case
    can be told apart by how much of each the memory itself writes. Which of the two readings
    that is, is read from the memory rather than fixed here, because the memories write their
    answers in two different ways. A memory that writes the same string into answer after
    answer, or that writes its answers out of strings its own list carries, writes a list a new
    answer can be read from: there the support is the share of the answer's entries that list
    writes, and an answer whose every entry is one of its strings is fully supported. A memory
    whose answers are all different writes no such list -- no new answer can be one of its
    strings -- so there the support is the share of the answer's own text the memory's answers
    are made of, which is the only reading left of a memory that writes a style rather than a
    list.
